      "content": "Let me try to infuse a bit more warmth into the template, while still maintaining a professional tone. You know, like a well-crafted wooden spoon, passed down through generations of skilled cooks - it's all about the attention to detail.\n\nHere's a revised template:\n\n\"Dear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the status of your application for the Software Engineer position at [Company Name]. I want to start by expressing my sincere gratitude for the time and effort you invested in our interview process. Your passion for software engineering and your impressive skills truly shone through during our conversations.\n\nAfter careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose skills and fit for the role are a better match for our team at this time. Please know that this decision is in no way a reflection on your abilities or potential as a software engineer. You have a remarkable talent for coding, and I have no doubt that you will find a team that appreciates your unique strengths.\n\nI want to thank you again for your interest in joining our team and for sharing your story with us. We appreciate the opportunity to have met and learned more about your experience. If you have any questions or would like to discuss further, please don",
